    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001>
        <Title>Make Dropbox authorization recoverable</Title>
        <DependsOn />
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Request file scopes and a fresh approval, add safe optional browser selection, and retain desktop PKCE without a mandatory callback.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Add code-step retry and a full-screen scrollable authorization URL with compact bounds and cursor handling. Document configuration and distinguish the unconfirmed Safari/provider failure.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>go test ./internal/infra/dropbox ./internal/infra/tui/views</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>Implement snapshots and real Dropbox transfer</Title>
        <DependsOn>T-001</DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Add validated versioned snapshots with optional preferences and a model-specific remote state repository. Export in a read transaction and restore all workout data/preferences atomically while retaining local identities.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Select the latest linked account, decrypt only inside the adapter, refresh expired credentials and persist encrypted updates, and implement bounded upload/download at /trainlog.json with sanitized failures.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Wire application save/load handlers and bootstrap, and cover validation, absent preferences, atomic rollback, HTTP parameters, refresh, and failures with injected transports and temporary databases.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>go test ./internal/app/... ./internal/infra/persistence/sqlite ./internal/infra/dropbox ./cmd/cli</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>Wire records save/load and preserve navigation</Title>
        <DependsOn>T-002</DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Implement asynchronous s save and l load with progress, duplicate-operation prevention, edit isolation during transfers, success/failure feedback, and refreshed records after restore.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Preserve gs/ge and dialog/help/setup input; remove l from next-page keys, retain other page bindings, and show l - load / s - save in records and help.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Review intended rendering snapshots and verify restore refresh, selection retention, errors, keyboard ownership, and existing navigation.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
          <Command>go test ./internal/infra/tui/... ./cmd/cli</Command>
        </Verification>
      </T-003>
      <T-004>
        <Title>Reconcile durable state and run final evidence</Title>
        <DependsOn>T-003</DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Update scoped graph/verification entries and indexes, add M-INFRA-DROPBOX-STATE ownership and deterministic evidence, and preserve unrelated durable entries.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Run full tests, vet, formatting and selected final assertions, then mark applied and archive under the existing user instruction to archive completed GRACE work.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification>
